WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.568
Inbrev sorts the inbox
of a Swiss family practice,

2
00:00:04.568 --> 00:00:06.858
with Apertus, inside the practice.

3
00:00:07.458 --> 00:00:11.372
Every morning, a Swiss practice
assistant opens one inbox.

4
00:00:11.939 --> 00:00:17.595
Lab reports, refill requests,
insurer forms, faxes, in four languages.

5
00:00:18.196 --> 00:00:21.498
Almost all of it is protected
by professional secrecy.

6
00:00:22.098 --> 00:00:27.108
Swiss family doctors spend
9.5 hours a week on administration.

7
00:00:27.608 --> 00:00:29.798
One click sorts 30 messages.

8
00:00:30.398 --> 00:00:33.569
Inbrev does not rate
or rank clinical content.

9
00:00:34.029 --> 00:00:39.703
Any message that may need a clinician
leaves automation and goes to a person –

10
00:00:39.703 --> 00:00:41.376
no rank, no assessment.

11
00:00:41.976 --> 00:00:45.774
Everything else is sorted
by who handles it, and by when.

12
00:00:46.374 --> 00:00:51.828
Open the insurer fax: every field
carries the exact words it came from.

13
00:00:52.428 --> 00:00:55.593
When Inbrev isn't sure, it doesn't guess.

14
00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:59.388
It says: you decide.
French and Italian work the same way.

15
00:00:59.988 --> 00:01:05.041
A separate clinical mode adds
an urgency hint, for research only:

16
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:08.228
off by default, and not a medical device.

17
00:01:08.828 --> 00:01:13.909
Apertus and Inbrev run on a network
with no way out – we checked:

18
00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:17.192
every attempt to reach the internet fails.

19
00:01:17.792 --> 00:01:19.408
Inbrev keeps sorting.

20
00:01:20.008 --> 00:01:21.526
No server in the practice?

21
00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:25.002
The same container can
run at a Swiss provider,

22
00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:29.285
engaged by the practice as an auxiliary
bound to professional secrecy.

23
00:01:29.885 --> 00:01:34.275
On a first synthetic
test set of 180 messages,

24
00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:39.619
Inbrev routes 94 % correctly with 8B,
and 96 % with 70B.

25
00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:42.295
With a second symptom check,

26
00:01:42.295 --> 00:01:47.935
all 16 messages with clinical
content now leave automation.

27
00:01:48.535 --> 00:01:53.342
Inbrev. Your practice inbox,
sorted where it belongs:

28
00:01:53.342 --> 00:01:56.343
in the practice, or in the Swiss cloud.
